-- The checks: what the text says of the table, and what the table says of
-- itself.

-- Every month from January 2013 to August 2020, once and in order: the
-- months of the eligible retirees of the new §10(א)(1).
GIVEN r IS A `pensioners' coefficient row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the row's month` r IS
    `September 2016 salary month` (r's `last active year`) (r's `last active month`)

#ASSERT count `the coefficient table` EQUALS 92
#ASSERT map `the row's month` `the coefficient table` EQUALS map (GIVEN i YIELD `September 2016 salary month` 2013 1 PLUS i) (range 0 91)

-- A period's coefficient is printed for a month exactly when the period
-- has not ended before the month began.
GIVEN r IS A `pensioners' coefficient row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prints a coefficient exactly for the periods still running` r IS
        ((r's `X to 31.8.2016` EQUALS NOTHING) EQUALS (`the row's month` r GREATER THAN `September 2016 salary month` 2016 8))
    AND ((r's `X to 28.2.2017` EQUALS NOTHING) EQUALS (`the row's month` r GREATER THAN `September 2016 salary month` 2017 2))
    AND ((r's `X to 31.5.2019` EQUALS NOTHING) EQUALS (`the row's month` r GREATER THAN `September 2016 salary month` 2019 5))
    AND NOT (r's `X from 1.6.2019` EQUALS NOTHING)

#ASSERT all `prints a coefficient exactly for the periods still running` `the coefficient table`

-- The coefficient of a retiree on a day: the row of his last active month,
-- the column of the period the day is in.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `X, the coefficient for the retiree on` y m d IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `last active year` EQUALS y AND r's `last active month` EQUALS m) `the coefficient table`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        BRANCH
            IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2019) THEN r's `X from 1.6.2019`
            IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) THEN r's `X to 31.5.2019`
            IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) THEN r's `X to 28.2.2017`
            IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013) THEN r's `X to 31.8.2016`
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `X, the coefficient for the retiree on` 2014 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015) EQUALS JUST (19.92%)
#ASSERT `X, the coefficient for the retiree on` 2014 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2019) EQUALS JUST (21.43%)
#ASSERT `X, the coefficient for the retiree on` 2019 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2020) EQUALS JUST (4%)
#ASSERT `X, the coefficient for the retiree on` 2019 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2018) EQUALS NOTHING

-- No rule asks it, but the table shows its making: for a last month n
-- months into 2013, the first 29 rows print n/84 (a seven-year scale) to
-- the hundredth of a percent in every column; the first period stops at
-- 19.92% and the next two at 35.65%.
GIVEN i IS A NUMBER, x IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is n/84 for the row` i x IF
    x EQUALS JUST (`to the nearest` ((i PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 84) 0.0001)

#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD
                 CONSIDER drop i `the coefficient table`
                 WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `is n/84 for the row` i (r's `X to 31.8.2016`) OR i AT LEAST 16
                 WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE)
            (range 0 28)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `X to 31.8.2016` EQUALS NOTHING OR r's `X to 31.8.2016` AT MOST JUST (19.92%)) `the coefficient table`

-- F-ofek-hadash-march-2017-b's evidence: the annex sets a coefficient for a
-- 2013 retiree in a period when no shekel supplement was in force, so A in
-- force is nothing; the reading takes the full amount.
`the annex prices a period before any shekel supplement was paid` MEANS
        `X, the coefficient for the retiree on` 2013 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2014) EQUALS JUST (1.19%)
    AND `A in force on the day` (`a 2017 placement` TRUE TRUE 1) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2014) EQUALS 0
    AND `A, the full shekel supplement for the retiree's grade` (`a 2017 placement` TRUE TRUE 1) EQUALS 1074.37
#ASSERT `the annex prices a period before any shekel supplement was paid`
#ASSERT `Y, the increase of the determining salary under §10 as replaced in 2017` (1.19%) 1074.37 EQUALS 12.785003
